 "Volume": "音量",
 "Walk the timeline from top to bottom. Every work opens to its own page — what you are hearing, the world it came from, what to listen for — with links to hear it on <b>YouTube</b>, <b>Spotify</b>, <b>Apple Music</b> and the <b>Internet Archive</b>, and a <b>▶</b> that streams a free recording right here. <b>⏵ Radio</b> on any composer plays the journey onward from that stop. Gold <b>theory stops</b> teach you what to listen <i>for</i>, right when history invented it. This timeline is the classical spine; jazz, rock, folk and the rest are in <b>Works</b>, filtered by genre. Mark works <b>heard</b>, <b>studied</b> or <b>loved</b>; everything is tracked under <b>Progress</b>. One era shows at a time — pick it from the row of eras.": "从上到下走完时间线。每部作品都有自己的页面——你听到的是什么、它诞生的世界、聆听要点——并提供在 <b>YouTube</b>、<b>Spotify</b>、<b>Apple Music</b> 和 <b>Internet Archive</b> 上收听的链接，还有一个 <b>▶</b> 可直接在此播放免费录音。任何作曲家上的 <b>⏵ Radio</b> 会从该站继续播放旅程。金色的<b>乐理站</b>会在历史上该概念诞生之时，教你该听<i>什么</i>。这条时间线是古典音乐的主干；爵士、摇滚、民谣等在<b>作品</b>中，可按流派筛选。把作品标记为<b>已听</b>、<b>研读</b>或<b>喜爱</b>；一切都记录在<b>进度</b>下。一次只显示一个时期——从时期一行中选择。",
